language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Place n marks on an n x n grid, one per row and column, so that the vectors between all pairs of marks are different (Costas array).
given n : int(1..)
find costas : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(1..n)

branching on [costas]

such that
$ the marks use each row (value) exactly once: the columns carry a permutation of 1..n
allDiff(costas),
$ for each distance l, the differences between marks l apart are all different (the difference triangle has no repeated value in any line)
forAll l : int(1..n-1) . allDiff([costas[i] - costas[i+l] | i : int(1..n-l)])
